WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:06.440
Tesla's $10 billion Texas solar cell factory marks its largest energy hardware bet yet, separate

00:00:06.440 --> 00:00:14.660
from vehicle production. This is Tesla Shorts Time, Episode 565. Tesla plans a $10 billion solar

00:00:14.660 --> 00:00:20.720
cell factory in Fort Bend County. The project targets Fort Bend County as part of expanded

00:00:20.720 --> 00:00:27.300
Texas manufacturing. It focuses on solar cell production capacity. The move adds a dedicated

00:00:27.300 --> 00:00:33.640
energy hardware line alongside existing vehicle and battery work. Construction plans emphasize

00:00:33.640 --> 00:00:39.780
large-scale output to support growing demand for solar plus storage systems. The facility

00:00:39.780 --> 00:00:45.620
will integrate with Tesla's broader energy ecosystem in the state. Production of the updated

00:00:45.620 --> 00:00:52.320
Megapack 3 started at a new Texas facility. The line aims for 50 gigawatt hours yearly energy

00:00:52.320 --> 00:00:59.240
storage capacity. This expands utility scale offerings beyond current Megapack volumes. The

00:00:59.240 --> 00:01:05.960
new design improves energy density and installation speed for large grid projects. Early output will

00:01:05.960 --> 00:01:11.860
support utility contracts already in backlog. While Tesla's scale's energy hardware on the

00:01:11.860 --> 00:01:17.600
ground, its autonomy efforts are showing they can run around the clock. Tesla Robotaxi service

00:01:17.600 --> 00:01:23.620
remained active at 9.25 pm with a 5 minute pickup estimate in Central Dallas and Highland

00:01:23.620 --> 00:01:29.200
Park. Fast, late evening availability points to efficient fleet distribution across the

00:01:29.200 --> 00:01:35.940
area. This demonstrates the system can sustain low weight times outside daytime peaks. The observation

00:01:35.940 --> 00:01:41.920
aligns with yesterday's coverage of Robotaxi expansion by confirming consistent coverage during

00:01:41.920 --> 00:01:47.880
off-peak hours. Passengers gain a practical low weight option for nighttime travel without

00:01:47.880 --> 00:01:54.780
slow down concerns. A video captured the Optimus Robot handling an unexpected interaction at a popcorn

00:01:54.780 --> 00:02:01.180
stand. The clip spread quickly online after the event. It offers a public look at how the

00:02:01.180 --> 00:02:07.260
humanoid responds to unstructured real world situations. The response highlighted the robot's

00:02:07.260 --> 00:02:13.740
ability to process surprise inputs without predefined scripts. Viewers noted the natural flow of

00:02:13.740 --> 00:02:20.080
the exchange in a casual dining setting. As the Robotaxi network proves it can operate continuously,

00:02:20.520 --> 00:02:26.240
attention is turning to how the underlying FSD system makes decisions without constant driver input.

00:02:27.040 --> 00:02:34.200
Tesla just confirmed Max speed control is not coming back to FSD. Tesla's AI chief stated that

00:02:34.200 --> 00:02:40.160
manual Max speed settings will not return. The system will instead learn preferred speeds from

00:02:40.160 --> 00:02:46.720
driver behavior. The change removes a previous user adjustable parameter in favor of observed patterns.

00:02:47.440 --> 00:02:53.540
Future updates will refine speed selection based on accumulated trip data. Drivers can influence

00:02:53.540 --> 00:03:00.040
outcomes only by demonstrating consistent choices over multiple drives. That same philosophy of learning

00:03:00.040 --> 00:03:05.620
from real behavior shows up in a special first principles look at what this change really means for

00:03:05.620 --> 00:03:13.040
the autonomy program. Tesla's decision to learn driver speed preferences directly from observed behavior

00:03:13.040 --> 00:03:18.840
rather than offering a manual Max speed slider removes one layer of explicit user control.

00:03:19.400 --> 00:03:24.800
The system now treats past driving patterns as the primary input for future speed decisions,

00:03:24.800 --> 00:03:30.740
shifting the interface from settings to implicit training data. This approach reduces the number

00:03:30.740 --> 00:03:36.480
of parameters a driver must manage, but also means any change in preference requires repeated

00:03:36.480 --> 00:03:42.940
demonstration rather than a single adjustment. Over time the model builds a personalized profile that

00:03:42.940 --> 00:03:50.000
reflects actual highway and city habits instead of one time inputs. The change carries direct consequences

00:03:50.000 --> 00:03:56.740
for how Tesla captures and monetizes driver data. Each mile driven under supervision becomes additional

00:03:56.740 --> 00:04:02.600
training material that refines the speed model for that specific account, potentially increasing the

00:04:02.600 --> 00:04:09.160
value of continued subscription access over one time purchases. At the same time the method places

00:04:09.160 --> 00:04:15.260
heavier weight on the quality and diversity of early fleet behavior since outliers in the initial

00:04:15.260 --> 00:04:21.260
data set can shape outcomes for later users who never set an explicit preference. Revenue

00:04:21.260 --> 00:04:26.520
recognition therefore tilts toward recurring engagement rather than upfront feature unlocks.

00:04:27.120 --> 00:04:33.820
Paul Graham described his wife's initial supervised FSD ride in strong terms. The comment highlights

00:04:33.820 --> 00:04:39.700
user reactions to recent software versions. It adds to public discussion around how the system

00:04:39.700 --> 00:04:46.000
performs in everyday conditions. The account focused on smooth handling of complex urban scenarios

00:04:46.000 --> 00:04:52.080
without intervention. Observers noted the shift in perception from cautious testing to routine

00:04:52.080 --> 00:04:58.780
reliance. While Tesla refines how its vehicles learn, it is also extending warranties on hardware

00:04:58.780 --> 00:05:05.000
that has already reached customers. Tesla acknowledged a power conversion system issue affecting

00:05:05.000 --> 00:05:10.560
cyber truck units. The company extended the warranty on the affected component to eight years.

00:05:11.220 --> 00:05:17.080
Owners now have clearer coverage terms for a known hardware problem. The extension applies across

00:05:17.080 --> 00:05:22.820
the current production run and addresses reported failures in the field. Service centers have begun

00:05:22.820 --> 00:05:28.740
outreach to schedule inspections for impacted vehicles. A firmware update began rolling out to

00:05:28.740 --> 00:05:33.660
portable mobile connector charging units. The change targets hardware that has seen

00:05:33.660 --> 00:05:39.300
infrequent software attention. It improves reliability for owners who rely on the portable

00:05:39.300 --> 00:05:45.700
chargers. The update addresses connectivity and safety features in the field. Owners can expect

00:05:45.700 --> 00:05:51.780
better performance during home and travel charging sessions. Hardware fixes are one side of the

00:05:51.780 --> 00:05:59.020
customer experience. Software and app updates are the other. Buyers of the Model YL received vehicles

00:05:59.020 --> 00:06:04.720
missing the cooled charger that had been part of the announced specifications. The omission leaves

00:06:04.720 --> 00:06:10.900
owners without a feature intended for extended travel comfort. Tesla has not yet clarified whether

00:06:10.900 --> 00:06:16.840
the hardware will be added later or if the original promise has changed. The discrepancy affects

00:06:16.840 --> 00:06:22.780
customer expectations around long distance capability and may prompt service requests once the issue

00:06:22.780 --> 00:06:31.080
becomes more widely known. Version 4.59.5 adds pet mode live activity support for Android users.

00:06:31.720 --> 00:06:37.600
It also introduces Tesla assist features that handle photos and maintain conversation context.

00:06:38.380 --> 00:06:44.600
The update expands in app capabilities for vehicle monitoring and assistance. Live activity keeps

00:06:44.600 --> 00:06:50.900
temperature and status visible without opening the full app. Continued conversations allow follow-up

00:06:50.900 --> 00:06:57.200
questions within the same thread. On the infrastructure side, Tesla is still adding new places to charge.

00:06:57.840 --> 00:07:04.860
The first 7-11 location with Tesla Superchargers opened in Japan. The site adds public charging access

00:07:04.860 --> 00:07:11.220
at a retail chain. It extends the network into new high traffic spots outside traditional highway

00:07:11.220 --> 00:07:18.100
corridors. Drivers can now charge while shopping at convenience stores in urban areas. The installation

00:07:18.100 --> 00:07:23.740
marks an expansion of the Supercharger footprint in the Japanese market. Dutch authorities

00:07:23.740 --> 00:07:30.960
agreed to withhold certain FSD data following Tesla's request. The decision limits public access

00:07:30.960 --> 00:07:36.460
to information regulators would normally release. It affects transparency around supervised

00:07:36.460 --> 00:07:42.700
autonomy testing in Europe. The request covers detailed performance metrics collected during European

00:07:42.700 --> 00:07:49.180
operations. Regulators cited the company's preference for confidentiality in ongoing evaluations.

00:07:49.800 --> 00:07:54.540
The company asked regulators to keep full self-driving test information confidential.

00:07:55.320 --> 00:08:00.740
The request limits what details reach the public record. It affects how oversight of supervised

00:08:00.740 --> 00:08:06.480
autonomy will proceed in the region. European authorities had planned broader disclosure of

00:08:06.480 --> 00:08:12.380
performance and incident data. Tesla cited competitive and safety considerations in its formal

00:08:12.380 --> 00:08:18.360
submission. While Tesla pushes its own robot and energy programs, other companies are entering

00:08:18.360 --> 00:08:25.260
the same spaces. Mitsubishi announced plans to produce humanoid robots at a rate of 1,000 units per

00:08:25.260 --> 00:08:31.180
month. The effort positions the company as a new entrant alongside Tesla's Optimus program.

00:08:31.760 --> 00:08:37.840
It adds competitive pressure on manufacturing scale and cost targets. The initial focus includes

00:08:37.840 --> 00:08:44.260
industrial and service applications where repetitive tasks dominate. Production ramp timelines aim

00:08:44.260 --> 00:08:51.480
to match growing demand for affordable humanoid platforms. BYD reported record July sales amid

00:08:51.480 --> 00:08:58.200
ongoing global EV market growth. Tesla continues development on FSD version 14.

00:08:58.720 --> 00:09:04.380
The contrast shows differing paths between volume sales and software focused autonomy efforts.

00:09:05.100 --> 00:09:11.120
BYD's monthly figures reflect strong domestic and export demand for its battery electric lineup.

00:09:11.920 --> 00:09:17.860
Tesla's emphasis remains on iterative software releases that improve supervised driving capabilities.

00:09:18.660 --> 00:09:23.140
The facility will use natural gas power plants rather than solar arrays.

00:09:24.020 --> 00:09:29.900
The choice separates the project from Tesla Energy Hardware. It raises questions about internal

00:09:29.900 --> 00:09:36.140
alignment on clean power sourcing for large compute builds. Construction timelines prioritize

00:09:36.140 --> 00:09:42.440
rapid deployment of generation capacity over renewable integration. The decision affects how the

00:09:42.440 --> 00:09:49.420
site will meet its projected terawatt scale compute output. Before we go, the next round of FSD version

00:09:49.420 --> 00:09:54.960
14 testing data should clarify how the learned speed model performs in varied conditions.

